    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS, all tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `bulkSignupWarning` in owner responses: `true` when more than 80 owners already share the responded owner's registration day, otherwise `false`.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`DailyRegistrations.java`** (new helper) \u2014 owns the day-count logic: `countOn(repo, day)` and `isBulkSignup(repo, day)` (threshold 80). This is the \"same accumulation path\" the daily-limit rule uses.\n\n2. **`EnsureDailyLimit.java`** \u2014 refactored to reuse `DailyRegistrations.countOn(...)` instead of its own inline loop over `findAll()`, removing the duplication.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `bulkSignupWarning` boolean to the `Owner` schema (generates `OwnerDto.setBulkSignupWarning(...)`).\n\n4. **`RespondWithOwner`, `RespondWithOwnerCreated`, `RespondWithOwnerUpdated`** \u2014 each now sets `bulkSignupWarning` on the DTO via the shared helper, so every single-owner response (GET/POST/PUT) carries the flag.\n\nDesign notes: the flag is a response-time computed value (not a persisted owner property), so it lives in the responders, with the counting logic factored into one small single-responsibility helper reused by the daily-limit rule. The threshold (80) sits below the hard daily create limit (100), so the warning flags a busy day before the day closes to further creates.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreNoBulkWarningUnderThreshold` passes (fresh create \u2192 `false`), and the full suite is green.",
